BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Metrotrails Hiking
UID:event_316390728@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041735Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260913T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260913T182000
SUMMARY:North Pocono Happy Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us on this point-to-point hike\, tracing historic Rail lines and othe
 r interesting and random stuff through the Northern tier of the Pocono Mou
 ntains.\nWe meet on the Old State Road at the trailhead for the North Poco
 no Rail Trail.\nFrom here\, we will head West and shuttle with his few car
 s as possible to our start.\nfrom there\, we will meander along some aband
 oned railroad beds\, as well as some old turnpike routes\, with only very 
 short bits of road between.\nThere may be one bridge on the way those with
  height issues won't like.\nAside from that\, the route is almost entirely
  clear and easy. Some might have uneven service\, and only about 3 mi is i
 mproved surface.\nEveryone should come prepared with everything they need 
 because we are only passing by one location where we can refill on any foo
 d or drink.Distance is about 15 mi.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 837
 4
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/316390728/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260902T202758Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260902T202758Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Metrotrails Hiking
UID:event_316331862@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041735Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260920T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260920T180000
SUMMARY:Schuylkill River Special Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this very interesting point to point hike in our Schuylkill Ri
 ver series! Distance will be about 15 miles and feature the Schuylkill Riv
 er Trail\, but also a lot of very interesting other things....\nAfter meet
 ing at the Schuylkill River Trail/Bartrum Trailhead on Market Street next 
 to the Dry Wall place in Auburn PA\, we will shuttle with as few vehicles 
 as possible to the beginning.\nThe hike will begin covering the trail syst
 em at Kaercher Creek Park\, which we've never visited before.\nWe'll weave
  around on most of their entire trail system\, and then make our way throu
 gh ball fields\, and into downtown Hamburg.\nWe'll get on the Schuylkill R
 iver Trail here and mostly follow it back to Auburn area\, but with some s
 urprise side trips along the way.\nOne of the side trips will include lock
 s and towpath on the Schuylkill Navigation that will be an out and back.\n
 Most of the route will be pretty easy. The first bit will have a little bi
 t of foot path\, and one of the side trips may have some weeds\, but nothi
 ng too terrible.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 8374
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/316331862/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260829T231231Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260829T231231Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Metrotrails Hiking
UID:event_316424285@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041735Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T183000
SUMMARY:Boonton Area Loop Hike and Railroad History Visit
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this loop hike around Boonton NJ area\, which will feature par
 ks we have done as well as not done\, connected by short back street jaunt
 s.\nThe main theme is that we will walk to and through the Tri State Railw
 ay Historical Society Open House day\, featuring a huge collection of vint
 age rail stuff!\nAfter we meet at the Acme\, we'll walk back streets and f
 ields to the event to arrive shortly after it starts.\nThen after we spend
  an hour or so there\, we'll continue on some different community trails. 
 We will weave through and cover as much of this as possible that we have n
 ot done before\, as well as ones we have such as the Trolley Trail and the
  Tourne.\nHow much of the stuff we do will depending on how we are doing o
 n mileage and how much daylight we have.\nWe may adjust our route along th
 e way. Planned route is about 15 miles.\nCost for entry is $10 at the door
  for adults or $8 online preordered.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 83
 74
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/316424285/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260904T232331Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T232331Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Metrotrails Hiking
UID:event_316396079@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041735Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T084500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T184500
SUMMARY:Jersey Central Farewell Summer Shore Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this point to point hike in the north NJ shore region.\nThe th
 eme of this one is of course the end of Summer\, but also the historic Cen
 tral Railroad of New Jersey.\nThe CNJ served a lot of shore points\, and i
 t's always fun to visit them on the hikes. So\, for this one\, we will foc
 us on some of these rights of ways\, including ones on the beach.\nAfter m
 eeting at the end point. Lot C at Sandy Hook\, we will shuttle with as few
  vehicles as possible to a point south of Red Bank where there was a junct
 ion with the New York and Long Branch line.\nThe CNJ had a line to the eas
 t from here\, which served Port Monmouth and continued east to a junction 
 with the Seashore Branch.\nWe will trace this as closely as possible. Some
  bits of it are now trail\, but they are very short. Some bits are now par
 king lots\, gas lines\, or roads. The route will take us through the racew
 ay area\, and then out toward the shore line.\nWe'll continue north follow
 ing the rail grade as closely as possible\, and eventually it turns into a
  walkway along the sea wall.\nWe'll continue on that walkway to the north 
 to Sandy Hook\, and probably at some point head to the water for a couple 
 of breaks before the end.\nThere will be places for food and drinks along 
 the way.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 8374
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/316396079/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260903T021737Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T021737Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
